## Summary

Prepared release 1.6 from release 1.5 (e3abe47) to prevent the old media worker from overwriting derived references during the separate CONTENT migration. Photo workers now own only originals beginning photos/; recording workers own only pronunciation/ originals. Prefix gates cover staged triggers, committed inbox decisions, startup queues and execution.

Initially implemented the brief's same-byte hash comparison. Ian explicitly replaced that design with ownership based on the current original cell's prefix; the hash machinery was removed. All CONTENT originals are intentionally left alone, including different-byte originals and crop changes. Old-style changes still request processing, and removing a recording original still clears output. A review finding requesting restoration of hash comparisons was declined because it relied on the superseded requirement.

Tests cover actual staged writes and committed inbox deliveries for PHOTO, PERSON and GROUP, same/different hash migrations, crop edits, old-style changes, insertion/deletion and execution guards. Database tests under timeout 30 and go vet ./... pass. Main was already up to date when merged before landing.

No production migration or deployment was performed. The original CONTENT migration task and worktree were left untouched; Ian deploys the interim release before rerunning that migration.

